WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.330
SPEAKER 1: Welcome to
the AI tool in Lucid.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:07.530
This first section is going to
cover creating diagrams straight

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:10.320
from text prompts, the most
basic use case for an AI tool

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.690
in a diagramming app
like Lucidchart.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.010
To access this tool,
you'll want to go

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:18.240
to the Lucid AI Prompt Editor,
right up at the top left here,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.730
where you'll have access to
the text editor right here

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.100
that you can paste
in your context.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.930
I'm just going to copy and
paste this prompt here,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:25.920
and this is a basic prompt

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.830
to create a project management
process flow chart.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.160
We're only covering the highest
level basic activities here.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.240
This will work like any
other LLM or AI design tool

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.290
for these prompts where the
more context and specifics

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.210
that you give it, the
better it will be able

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.520
to respond to your approvals.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.920
If not, if you just have
something basic like this,

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.250
we'll create some steps
that would make sense

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:54.870
for a high-level process such
as a project management flow.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:58.530
So as we can see here, this
is a pretty logical flow.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.370
You can follow a lot of the
statements or if/then branches

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:07.860
that we've created and revise
manually as needed from here.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.470
This'll be put into
a default layout,

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.360
assisted layout container
for you in Lucid,

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.160
so you can edit these
shapes, move them around,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.400
and our arrows will rearrange
themselves accordingly for you.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.160
And this should get rid of
a lot of that manual work

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:21.660
for many team members that have

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.220
to create these
diagrams from scratch.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.980
These rough drafts are going to
save you a lot of time here.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.890
You can also access the
tool at this toolbar

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:31.860
to update nodes or decisions.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:36.540
So if you wanted to add a step,
remove a step, or change some

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:37.710
of the flow, change how some

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:40.980
of the if/then statements are
supposed to happen or branches,

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.240
you can do that in
this tool as well.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.600
You don't have to do
it just manually here.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.740
Now diagram types that we
support range very widely,

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.350
and that's a great use case for
so many different teams here.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.960
So let's go over a few other
different diagram types

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.700
that we are going to excel at.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.440
Right here is a BPMN
choreography diagram.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.090
We support BPMN choreography

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.610
and sequence diagrams
directly in the tool.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:09.780
And so this prompt generated
a diagram just like this one

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.170
